  "result": "I've written the plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\add-a-new-parameter-valiant-bunny.md`. I haven't edited any code, since plan mode is on. The tool for formally requesting plan approval isn't available here, so I'm asking in text instead.\n\n**Plan**\n- **`src/click/types.py`:** add `class KeyValue(ParamType[tuple[str, str]])` next to `UUIDParameterType`.\n  - It splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n  - Input with no `=`, or with an empty key (`=v`), calls `self.fail(\"{value!r} is not a valid key=value pair.\")`.\n  - A value that is already a tuple is passed through unchanged.\n- **`src/click/__init__.py`:** export `KeyValue`.\n- **Docs:** add an `autoclass` entry for it in `docs/api.md`, and a changelog line in `CHANGES.md`.\n- **Tests:** add cases to `tests/test_types.py` for valid input, a value containing `=`, an empty value, and both failure modes. The failure cases check the exit code and the message text, run through `CliRunner` with `@click.option(\"--set\", type=click.KeyValue())`.\n\nI'll check it by running `pytest` on the types and info-dict tests, then the full suite.\n\nShall I go ahead and implement it?",
